(386, 46, '_academia_syllabus', 'Framing the subject::Terminology and the mental model everyone needs first;Where this sits in the wider operating model;What good looks like — and how it is measured§Current-state diagnostic::Assessing your organisation against the standard;Identifying the three gaps that matter most;Building the baseline you will report against§Roles, accountability and decision rights::Who decides what, and on what evidence;RACI in practice without the bureaucracy;Escalation paths that actually get used§Planning and prioritisation::Sequencing work against capacity, not ambition;Trade-off frameworks for competing demands;Making the plan survive first contact§Working with stakeholders::Mapping influence and interest;Structuring a difficult conversation;Communicating status without spin§Performance and measurement::Choosing metrics that change behaviour;Leading versus lagging indicators;Reporting to a board audience§Common failure modes::The five mistakes practitioners see most often;Early warning signs and how to read them;Recovering a programme that has drifted§Embedding it at work::Stakeholder map and the first three conversations;30/60/90-day action plan built in the room;Using the toolkit: templates, checklists and calculators'),
